    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. The only test classes in the project are in the `acceptance` package, and `BUILD SUCCESS` with all tests green confirms the change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented locality derivation from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\nThe `locality` field is a **derived, read-only response field** \u2014 same pattern as the existing `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, and `membershipTier` fields. It's not stored on the entity; it's computed when an `Owner` is mapped to an `OwnerDto` on GET/POST responses. Two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `locality` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` to `toOwnerDto`, plus a fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `locality(owner)` method that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 Sydney gives `NSW`; `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 random city gives `UNKNOWN`) pass, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
